<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cayuga people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cayuga Nation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cayuga are an Iroquoian people, one of the five original nations of the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) Confederacy, whose homeland lay around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayuga-lake">Cayuga Lake</a> in the Finger Lakes region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>. They held ten of the fifty chiefly titles in the confederacy's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a>. Most sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a> and lost their lands, and today they live at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-nations-of-the-grand-river">Six Nations of the Grand River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, in New York and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oklahoma">Oklahoma</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cayuga-people.jpg" alt="Cayuga people" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cayuga_Leaders_-_Iroquois_Past_and_Present.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Together they persuaded the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, <b>Cayuga</b> and Seneca to accept the Great Law of Peace, the Gayanashagowa, and finally won over the feared Onondaga chief Tadodaho, whose name became the title of the league’s presiding chief.</blockquote><a href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>A <b>Cayuga Nation</b> survives in New York.</blockquote><a href="/state/cayuga-nation">Cayuga Nation</a></li></ul></section>
